**Caution**
The Issues are strictly limited for the reporting of problem encountered with the software provided in this project.
For any other problem related to the STM32 product, the performance, the hardware characteristics and boards, the tools the environment in general, please post a topic in the [ST Community/STM32 MCUs forum](https://community.st.com/s/group/0F90X000000AXsASAW/stm32-mcus) 

**Describe the set-up**
In stm32h7xx_ll_tim.h, there are many instances of doing the following:
WRITE_REG(register, ~(bit))
Where it could be a lot better to use:
CLEAR_BIT(register, bit)

There is also a lot of casting from a pointer to uint32_t, which has been fixed for compiling the headers in 64 bit mode by previously defining all instances of uint32_t to size_t. Which isn't an ideal fix.

It is specially an issue for metaprogramming purposes (shown below)

**Additional context**
This is a small problem when trying to use the LL headers to do testing on non STM hardware (64-bit), as shown below:
```c
#ifndef STM32H7xx_LL_TIM_WRAPPER_H
#define STM32H7xx_LL_TIM_WRAPPER_H

#include <stddef.h>

#include "MockedDrivers/stm32h723xx_wrapper.h"

#include "stm32h7xx.h"

#include "MockedDrivers/mocked_ll_tim.hpp"

// -Woverflow does not do much in stm32h7xx_ll_tim.h
// the only places where it's used in are in WRITE_REG(reg, ~(bit))
// where they should use CLEAR_BIT(reg, bit)
#pragma GCC diagnostic push
#pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Woverflow"
#define uint32_t size_t
#include "stm32h7xx_ll_tim.h"
#undef uint32_t
#pragma GCC diagnostic pop

#include "MockedDrivers/common.hpp"

#endif // STM32H7xx_LL_TIM_WRAPPER_H
```

**Suggested fix**
 - Try to compile the headers in 64 bit mode and see all the warnings when defining uint32_t -> size_t. This will show every instance of WRITE_REG(register, ~(bit)), then exchange it with CLEAR_BIT(register, bit).
 - Try to compile the headers in 64 bit mode without any changes to find every instance of uint32_t being used as a address size then change each to size_t.

If the changes have been applied correctly, the wrapper should not need any redefinitions:
```c
#ifndef STM32H7xx_LL_TIM_WRAPPER_H
#define STM32H7xx_LL_TIM_WRAPPER_H

#include <stddef.h>

#include "MockedDrivers/stm32h723xx_wrapper.h"

#include "stm32h7xx.h"

#include "MockedDrivers/mocked_ll_tim.hpp"

#include "stm32h7xx_ll_tim.h"

#include "MockedDrivers/common.hpp"

#endif // STM32H7xx_LL_TIM_WRAPPER_H
```

