Working on the mbed-ce/mbed-os DMA SPI code for STM32H7, I observed that my code was going into the DMA error ISR handler during DMA transfers.  This happened intermittently and for no apparent reason, and the error bit was the FIFO error flag.  Eventually I found [this forum thread](https://community.st.com/t5/stm32-mcus-touchgfx-and-gui/spi-dma-error-is-occurred-when-the-other-dma-memory-to-memory-is/td-p/191590) that described the issue and the fix well.  Basically, the FIFO error flag can set under "nominal" conditions just due to the DMA controller having issues acquiring the MCU internal bus.  

