In my case SPI master transmits data with long data blocks (~16bytes) and pretty fast (SCK=8MHz). I am interested with first three bytes only. So just run HAL_SPI_TransmitReceive() with length=3. And from time to time I got two bytes in FIFO. Sometimes it results with hspi->RxXferCount underflow here:
https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32h7xx_hal_driver/blob/d8461b980b59b1625207d8c4f2ce0a9c2a7a3b04/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_spi.c#L1459

When it happens loop here makes much more data is received and copied to user buffer.
https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32h7xx_hal_driver/blob/d8461b980b59b1625207d8c4f2ce0a9c2a7a3b04/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_spi.c#L1409

All of that results with HardFault (BusFault, IMPRECISERR) in my case.

I think there shall be check about underflow in here:
https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32h7xx_hal_driver/blob/d8461b980b59b1625207d8c4f2ce0a9c2a7a3b04/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_spi.c#L1418
